  "details": "This is important for index users, as the index's joystick has a design flaw that can cause the touch cable to break with prolonged and repeated use of the joystick\n\nProvide a button that can be bound to move and rotate\n\nFor example, when pressing the A button, it rotates at a certain angle or moves in the third person ,similar to [Hot Dogs, Horseshoes & Hand Grenades]\n\nThis would minimize the use of joysticks\n\nAlso would like to see the pressure feedback of index used to bind function buttons as well, e.g. pressing the touchpad hard enough to disable voice mute........",
